Maven Integration:

Install Maven Plugin in Jenkins
- Go to Manage Jenkins
- Click on Plugins → Available Plugins
- Search for Maven Plugins and Click on Install
Maven Setup in Jenkins and Configuring the Maven tool:
- Go to Manage Jenkins → Global Tool Configuration → Maven
- Click Add Maven, give it a name and version
- Click Apply and Save
Example job configuration:
- Click New Item, give it a name, click OK
- Go to Configuration → Source Code Management → select Git → provide the repository URL
- Go to Build → Invoke top-level Maven targets
- Provide the Maven version and set the goal as install
- Click Apply and Save
- Click Build Now and check the console output
